---
/**
 * Track 4 (Visual Math: Linear Algebra), Lesson 15, illustration 2 of 2.
 *
 * The derivative is a matrix in the basis {1, x, x², x³}. The matrix D
 * sends column k+1 (the basis vector x^k) to the column representing
 * k·x^(k-1): D = [[0, 1, 0, 0], [0, 0, 2, 0], [0, 0, 0, 3], [0, 0, 0, 0]].
 * Applied to [7, 5, 2, 0] (the polynomial 2x² + 5x + 7) it gives
 * [5, 4, 0, 0] (the polynomial 4x + 5), exactly the derivative.
 */

const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="la-deriv-title la-deriv-desc">
		<title id="la-deriv-title">The derivative operator is a matrix in the basis 1, x, x², x³</title>
		<desc id="la-deriv-desc">A typeset matrix equation. The 4 by 4 matrix D equals [[0, 1, 0, 0], [0, 0, 2, 0], [0, 0, 0, 3], [0, 0, 0, 0]] in purple multiplies the 4 by 1 column [7, 5, 2, 0] also in purple, producing the 4 by 1 column [5, 4, 0, 0]. Polynomial annotations to the right read: input column = 2 x squared plus 5 x plus 7 (in teal), and output column = 4 x plus 5 (in amber). The label below confirms that D times the coordinate vector is exactly the derivative.</desc>

		<text x="370" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>derivative as matrix multiplication</text>

		{/* matrix D */}
		<g transform="translate(40, 90)">
			<text x="0" y="100" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="160" font-weight="200" fill={ACCENT}>[</text>
			<g font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>
				<text x="38" y="42">0</text><text x="68" y="42">1</text><text x="98" y="42">0</text><text x="128" y="42">0</text>
				<text x="38" y="72">0</text><text x="68" y="72">0</text><text x="98" y="72">2</text><text x="128" y="72">0</text>
				<text x="38" y="102">0</text><text x="68" y="102">0</text><text x="98" y="102">0</text><text x="128" y="102">3</text>
				<text x="38" y="132">0</text><text x="68" y="132">0</text><text x="98" y="132">0</text><text x="128" y="132">0</text>
			</g>
			<text x="160" y="100" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="160" font-weight="200" fill={ACCENT}>]</text>
			<text x="105" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">D (derivative matrix)</text>
		</g>

		{/* multiplication dot */}
		<text x="260" y="195" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="32" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>·</text>

		{/* input column [7, 5, 2, 0] */}
		<g transform="translate(290, 100)">
			<text x="0" y="92" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="140" font-weight="200" fill={TEAL}>[</text>
			<g font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>
				<text x="32" y="40">7</text>
				<text x="32" y="70">5</text>
				<text x="32" y="100">2</text>
				<text x="32" y="130">0</text>
			</g>
			<text x="62" y="92" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="140" font-weight="200" fill={TEAL}>]</text>
			<text x="45" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill={TEAL}>2x²+5x+7</text>
		</g>

		{/* equals sign */}
		<text x="415" y="195" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>=</text>

		{/* output column [5, 4, 0, 0] */}
		<g transform="translate(450, 100)">
			<text x="0" y="92" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="140" font-weight="200" fill={AMBER}>[</text>
			<g font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>
				<text x="32" y="40">5</text>
				<text x="32" y="70">4</text>
				<text x="32" y="100">0</text>
				<text x="32" y="130">0</text>
			</g>
			<text x="62" y="92" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="140" font-weight="200" fill={AMBER}>]</text>
			<text x="45" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill={AMBER}>4x+5</text>
		</g>

		{/* d/dx notation arrow */}
		<g transform="translate(560, 160)">
			<text x="0" y="0" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">in calculus:</text>
			<text x="0" y="22" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>d/dx (2x²+5x+7)</text>
			<text x="0" y="42" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>= 4x + 5</text>
			<text x="0" y="76" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">same thing, different language</text>
		</g>

		<text x="370" y="328" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.85">
			D · <tspan fill={TEAL} font-weight="700">[7, 5, 2, 0]</tspan> = <tspan fill={AMBER} font-weight="700">[5, 4, 0, 0]</tspan>: matrix multiplication IS differentiation here
		</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>In the basis 1, x, x², x³, the derivative becomes a matrix. The 4 by 4 D pulls each x^k entry into the k·x^(k-1) slot. Multiply D by the coordinate vector of 2x² + 5x + 7 and you get the coordinate vector of 4x + 5. The calculus rule and the matrix product are doing the same job.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
